 {
  "id": "more-loops",
  "title": "More loops",
  "summary": "Stop early, skip ahead, and put loops inside loops.",
  "symbol": "arrow.2.squarepath",
  "optional": false,
  "lessons": [
   {
    "id": "loop-break",
    "title": "Stop early with break",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "xp": 13,
    "terms": [
     {
      "word": "break",
      "meaning": "Stops a loop right away.",
      "like": "the emergency stop button on a treadmill."
     }
    ],
    "explanation": "break stops a loop right away, even if it had more laps to go. The program carries on after the loop.\n\nIt's often used with while True:, a loop that would run forever, plus an if that breaks out when it's time to stop.",
    "why": "while True means \"keep going,\" so the only way out is break. That's handy when you don't know ahead of time how many laps you need, like asking questions until someone types quit.",
    "exampleCode": "while True:\n    word = input(\"Say something (or quit): \")\n    if word == \"quit\":\n        break\n    print(\"You said\", word)\nprint(\"Bye!\")",
    "exampleNote": "Run it. Type a few words, then type quit.",
    "walkthrough": [
     {
      "code": "while True:",
      "note": "Keeps looping until something breaks out."
     },
     {
      "code": "word = input(\"Say something (or quit): \")",
      "note": "Asks each lap."
     },
     {
      "code": "if word == \"quit\":",
      "note": "Checks whether it's time to stop."
     },
     {
      "code": "break",
      "note": "Leaves the loop right away."
     },
     {
      "code": "print(\"Bye!\")",
      "note": "Runs after the loop."
     }
    ],
    "mistakes": [
     {
      "wrong": "for n in range(5):\n    print(n)\nbreak",
      "why": "break only works inside a loop. Indent it under an if inside the loop.",
      "fix": "for n in range(5):\n    print(n)\n    if n == 2:\n        break"
     }
    ],
    "practices": [
     {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "code",
      "prompt": "Fill in the blank so the loop stops when n reaches 3.",
      "starterCode": "for n in range(10):\n    if n == 3:\n        ___\n    print(n)",
